    <item ident="gd8277ffbfa5acb8c6fd48c9d91f44444" title="Web APIs">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_answers_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>9037,379,6648,8199</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A well-designed Web API should abstract away the complexities of the server-side implementation. &amp;nbsp;Users (developers) should be able to interact with the API without needing to understand the internal workings of the server.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which of the following statements is another characteristics of a &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;good &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;API?\&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Select all that apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Multiple">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="9037">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Clear and comprehensive documentation.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="379">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Returning data in a structured format like JSON or XML</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6648">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using standard HTTP methods like GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="8199">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Requiring developers to have extensive knowledge of the server-side implementation.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <and>
              <varequal respident="response1">9037</varequal>
              <varequal respident="response1">379</varequal>
              <varequal respident="response1">6648</varequal>
              <not>
                <varequal respident="response1">8199</varequal>
              </not>
            </and>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="g49ec045c5ca6bfffee2b8c6bd550a6e7" title="Window Object">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>8976,9072,9466,1247</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which of the following code snippets correctly retrieves the current page filename (assuming that it exists) from the URL using &lt;code&gt;window.location&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="8976">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">window.location.pathname.split("/").pop();</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="9072">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">window.location.hostname;</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="9466">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">window.location.filename;</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="1247">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">window.location.href.split('/').slice(-1)[0];</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8976</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="gb52aadf73e26420e05bc083ba4cc526d" title="null vs. undefined in async">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>5824,7919,8889,5214</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Given this code snippt which fetches data from a third-party API:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; url &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token operator"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token string"&gt;"https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/ditto"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; results &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token operator"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token function"&gt;getPokemon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token parameter"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;&amp;nbsp; const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; response &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token operator"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token function"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;&amp;nbsp; if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token comment"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; data &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token operator"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token function"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token function"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; doStuff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;&amp;nbsp; }&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;}&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token keyword"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token function"&gt;doStuff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token parameter"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;  results &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token operator"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;  console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token function"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token string"&gt;"first: "&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span class="token function"&gt;getPokemon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token function"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token string"&gt;"second: "&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="token punctuation"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why is a good idea to initialize the variable &lt;code&gt;results&lt;/code&gt; with the value of &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; versus being just &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="5824">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">JavaScript runs the getPokemon(url) asynchronously, so the console.log("second: ", results); at the end will likely run before the fetch operation completes. At this point, results is still null, showing that the data has not yet been fetched.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="7919">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The JavaScript will not run unless it is set to null. Not initializing the value causes an error when the second console log attempts to display the results.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="8889">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The output of the console.log("second: ", results); will never be updated given this code.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="5214">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Variables with undefined values produce a long message that is displayed to the user about the variable only being declared but not populated.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">5824</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
